<p>An optional callback to change the paint a text run draws with.</p>


<pre class="language-csharp"><code class="language-csharp">public Action&lt;SkiaSharp.SKPaint,IStyle,bool&gt; ConfigurePaint { get; set; }</code></pre>

<h2 id="remarks">Remarks</h2><pre class="language-txt"><code class="language-txt">        Called once per drawn run just before its text is drawn, with the run's
        text paint, the run's style and `false`, and again with the halo
        paint, the style and `true` for runs that have a halo.  The paint
        also draws the run's underline and strikethrough.  The paint is reset
        after each run, so changes (for example `Color` or
        `MaskFilter`) don't carry over.  Don't keep a reference to the paint.
        




        Background colors and the selection highlight aren't drawn with this
        paint, so they are unaffected.  For a shadow pass, use a separate
        options object with no [Selection](./../ref/Topten.RichTextKit.TextPaintOptions.Selection).
        




        The callback is called for every run on every paint, so create any
        Skia objects it uses (such as mask filters) once and reuse them,
        rather than creating them in the callback.
        
</code></pre>

